  "title": "Withdrawal Date, Safety, and Accommodation",
  "body": "Withdrawal Date, Safety, and Accommodation  Withdrawal Date  The deadline for withdrawing with a W grade is November 7 at 5:00 PM and is the responsibility of the student.   Accessibility, and Accommodation  If you need accommodations due to a learning, physical, or other disability you must present a memo to me from Student Accessibility Resources (SAR) indicating the existence of a disability and the suggested reasonable accommodations. If you have not already done so, please contact the Student Accessibility Resource (215 The Blue Connection), by calling 331-2490 or emailing access@gvsu.edu . Please note that I am unable to provide accommodations based upon disability until I have received a copy of the SAR issued memo. For more information visit .  Growth as a person does is certainly not limited to the classroom or academics. If there is an upcoming faith or religious observance that could have an impact on your attendance or work in the class, please submit a request during the first two weeks of the semester, or as soon as is reasonably possible, so that we can plan together accordingly.    Classroom and Campus Safety  I consider classroom and campus safety our shared responsibility. Please familiarize yourself with the classroom emergency placard, which contains important information that could prove useful should an emergency arise. Emergency situations could include a fire alarm, tornado warning, medical emergency, or hostile intruder, and our response might consist of evacuating the building in an orderly manner, moving as a group to a different location in the building, rendering assistance a class member, or staying put and locking the classroom door. In all cases, I will provide clear instructions as to what you should do.  Please make sure to have your primary mobile number listed in Banner so that you will automatically receive any campus alerts. Should you receive an emergency notification in class, notify me immediately.  You can find more information about campus safety can be found at the sites shown in .   Safety Information Locations     Information Resource Location  Directions for enabling additional contact means to the campus alert system  List of campus tornado safety locations   Active shooter response   Medical emergencies and campus AED locations      "
